                            <comment id="16103042" author="amashenkov" created="Thu, 27 Jul 2017 10:24:10 +0000"  >&lt;p&gt;Looks weird as BigDecimal test passes. See attached test to &lt;a href=&quot;https://issues.apache.org/jira/browse/IGNITE-5818&quot; title=&quot;SQL: query with condition on affinity column works incorrect in some cases.&quot; class=&quot;issue-link&quot; data-issue-key=&quot;IGNITE-5818&quot;&gt;&lt;del&gt;IGNITE-5818&lt;/del&gt;&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;</comment>
                            <comment id="16140229" author="ilyak" created="Thu, 24 Aug 2017 16:04:18 +0000"  >&lt;p&gt;The offender here is H2&apos;s ValueDecimal class:&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;It doesn&apos;t override Value&apos;s covertTo(), so when it is asked to be converted to Java object, it returns&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;code panel&quot; style=&quot;border-width: 1px;&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;codeContent panelContent&quot;&gt;
&lt;pre class=&quot;code-java&quot;&gt;                &lt;span class=&quot;code-keyword&quot;&gt;return&lt;/span&gt; ValueJavaObject.getNoCopy(&lt;span class=&quot;code-keyword&quot;&gt;null&lt;/span&gt;,
                        StringUtils.convertHexToBytes(getString().trim()), getDataHandler());
&lt;/pre&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Instead of sensible &quot;if (targetType == JAVA_OBJECT) return value;&quot; as one might imagine.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;So we will have to do the check outside of H2 code.&lt;/p&gt;</comment>
